    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **34 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\nThe implementation:\n\n1. **`Owner`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdMemberCount` field (mirroring the existing `namesakeCount` snapshot pattern), so the tier is derivable on every read, including a fresh `GET`.\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added `countHouseholdMembers(householdId)`, which counts existing owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` plus the owner itself (the \"after this create\" count), and set it on the owner during `addOwner`, right after `householdId` is computed.\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 `membershipTier` now returns `GOLD` when `householdMemberCount >= 3`, otherwise falls back to the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules.\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added the `household_member_count` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql).\n5. **openapi.yml** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nBecause household membership grows over time, the count is snapshotted at create time (like `namesakeCount`), so the tier reflects the household size at the moment of that owner's creation. The Cp23 test's third household member correctly resolves to `GOLD`, and the existing SILVER/BRONZE tests still pass.",
